  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing the urgent needs of migrants in situations of vulnerability in Thailand, affected by the crisis in Myanmar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The human security situation in Myanmar, combined with regional mobility trends, has reshaped and complicated the long-standing mobility between Myanmar and Thailand. People are moving because of immediate and urgent human security issues, be it political and personal insecurity or economic and food insecurity. In response, IOM proposes a two-pronged approach that addresses the immediate needs of the most vulnerable affected populations, while also working with policy makers and employers to improve existing regular pathways and working conditions for Myanmar nationals in Thailand. The approach aims to deliver people-centred, humanitarian assistance while also contributing to policy level initiatives to reduce vulnerabilities and protect the rights of migrants in Thailand.</narrative>
  </description>
